.TH WRIT\-COMPLETIONS 1 2026-10-12 "writ 0.1.0" "writ manual"
.SH NAME
writ\-completions \- print a shell completion script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nh
.ad l
\fBwrit completions\fR \fISHELL\fR
.ad
.hy
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a script that lets SHELL complete writ commands, options, and file names.
.PP
To load it, run the line for your shell, or add it to your shell's startup file (~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, or ~/.config/fish/config.fish):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
bash:  source <(writ completions bash)
zsh:   source <(writ completions zsh)        (after compinit)
fish:  writ completions fish | source
.fi
.RE
.PP
eval "$(writ completions SHELL)" works too, but only with the double quotes: without them, the shell joins the script into one line, and it does nothing.
.PP
To install the script as a file instead, which makes the shell start faster:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
bash:  writ completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/writ
zsh:   writ completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_writ
       (with fpath=(~/.zfunc $fpath) before compinit in ~/.zshrc)
fish:  writ completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/writ.fish
.fi
.RE
.PP
Packages install these files for you.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fISHELL\fR
bash, zsh, or fish
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help; \fB\-h\fR is short, \fB\-\-help\fR is long
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
success; for questions, the answer is yes
.TP
1
the answer is no: the check, verification, proof or name lookup was denied
.TP
2
an error: bad usage, unreadable input, or a failed operation
.SH EXAMPLES
Load completions in ~/.zshrc:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
autoload \-Uz compinit && compinit
source <(writ completions zsh)
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwrit\fR(1)
